# What `COPY . /app` must not bake into the image. `.gitignore` governs what
# reaches a commit; it does not reach the image. So this file is the guard
# DEPLOYMENT.md meant when it said a real `*.conf` "cannot be committed by
# reflex": that keeps one out of git, this keeps one out of the layer.

# Version control and CI: not runtime, and .git is large.
.git
.github

# Editor and tool state.
.idea
.vscode
.claude

# Editor backups and swap files. An `nginx.conf~` is a copy of a file the
# last section keeps out, under a name it does not match.
**/*~
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Local build output. The image compiles its own; a stale host .fasl must
# not shadow a fresh build. build.lisp writes an executable at the root, an
# SBCL core like any *.core, tens of megabytes the container never runs.
**/*.fasl
**/*.core
/web-skeleton

# The test suite: the demo system does not load it.
tests

# Secrets and real proxy configs carrying live hostnames. The sample ships as
# `nginx.conf.sample`, which ends in .sample and so is not matched by *.conf.
*.conf
**/*.conf
.env
.env.*
**/.env
